{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both tests pass. Here's the fix:\n\n```python\ndef truncate_slug(text, limit):\n    truncated = text[:limit]\n    # A cut can land right after a hyphen, leaving a dangling trailing \"-\".\n    # Strip it so the slug never ends with one.\n    return truncated.rstrip(\"-\")\n```\n\n**What was wrong:** `repo/slug.py`'s `truncate_slug` sliced the slug at `limit` but never removed a trailing hyphen. When a cut landed right after a `-` (e.g. `\"my-report-title\"` at 10 → `\"my-report-\"`), the report URL ended up with a dangling dash.\n\n**The fix:** after slicing, `rstrip(\"-\")` removes any trailing hyphen so slugs never end with one. This also keeps short, already-clean slugs (like `\"abc\"`) unchanged, matching the `test_short_unchanged` expectation.\n\nNote: I only touched the actual bug. I left the unrelated `TODO` comments in `slug.py`, `format.py`, and `rows.py` alone since they weren't part of this issue — happy to address any of them if you want."}]},"session_id":"2c0ecad8-06d5-4a75-889f-863195d7d3c8"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","duration_ms":27258,"duration_api_ms":27258,"is_error":false,"result":"The bug is in `truncate_slug` in `repo/slug.py` — it slices at the limit but doesn't strip a trailing hyphen, so `\"my-report-title\"` truncated to 10 chars becomes `\"my-report-\"` instead of `\"my-report\"`.Now let me verify the fix passes the tests:Both tests pass. Here's the fix:\n\n```python\ndef truncate_slug(text, limit):\n    truncated = text[:limit]\n    # A cut can land right after a hyphen, leaving a dangling trailing \"-\".\n    # Strip it so the slug never ends with one.\n    return truncated.rstrip(\"-\")\n```\n\n**What was wrong:** `repo/slug.py`'s `truncate_slug` sliced the slug at `limit` but never removed a trailing hyphen. When a cut landed right after a `-` (e.g. `\"my-report-title\"` at 10 → `\"my-report-\"`), the report URL ended up with a dangling dash.\n\n**The fix:** after slicing, `rstrip(\"-\")` removes any trailing hyphen so slugs never end with one. This also keeps short, already-clean slugs (like `\"abc\"`) unchanged, matching the `test_short_unchanged` expectation.\n\nNote: I only touched the actual bug. I left the unrelated `TODO` comments in `slug.py`, `format.py`, and `rows.py` alone since they weren't part of this issue — happy to address any of them if you want.","session_id":"2c0ecad8-06d5-4a75-889f-863195d7d3c8","request_id":"0a380f39-dc66-4ced-8d1c-8295561ea41b","usage":{"inputTokens":9405,"outputTokens":1141,"cacheReadTokens":111456,"cacheWriteTokens":0}}
